================================================================================================
AE SIGNAL AMPLITUDE — is P(good) Theta(1), or does Porter-Thomas kill it?
================================================================================================
  R=0.6, exact statevector. P(good) = P(x_i=1 AND Pauli_l = -1) on the
  W-gate state, block 0, averaged over qubits and over the group's terms.
  'max bitstring' is the largest single joint outcome probability - the
  quantity Porter-Thomas actually concentrates, shown for contrast.

    N  reps    M   n   P(x_i=1)  P(good) min  P(good) mean  max bitstring  unif 2^-(n+N)
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    4     1   16   4   0.500000     0.228090      0.300062      2.077e-02      3.906e-03
    4     2   24   4   0.500000     0.220938      0.277464      2.550e-02      3.906e-03
    4     3   32   4   0.500000     0.173216      0.219219      2.004e-02      3.906e-03
    4     4   40   4   0.500000     0.230313      0.259793      1.852e-02      3.906e-03
    4     5   48   4   0.500000     0.122642      0.207508      1.736e-02      3.906e-03
  ......................................................................................
    6     1   24   6   0.500000     0.090060      0.222602      1.742e-03      2.441e-04
    6     2   36   6   0.500000     0.141322      0.230370      3.113e-03      2.441e-04
    6     3   48   6   0.500000     0.188014      0.237923      1.910e-03      2.441e-04
    6     4   60   6   0.500000     0.222693      0.254576      2.044e-03      2.441e-04
    6     5   72   6   0.500000     0.204697      0.246777      2.278e-03      2.441e-04
  ......................................................................................

  P(good) holding near a constant as reps grows means AE's signal does NOT
  collapse and the Porter-Thomas caveat was aimed at the wrong object -
  bitstring probabilities concentrate, two-bit marginals do not. That
  closes action-plan item 3. It does NOT revive AE: the T2 forfeiture
  (Theta(M/eps) against Theta(1/eps^2)) is what demoted it, and that
  argument is untouched by this result.
